  "question": {
    "text": "An object of mass ' m ' is projected from origin in a vertical $x y$ plane at an angle $45^{\\circ}$ with the x axis with an initial velocity $\\mathrm{v}_0$. The magnitude and direction of the angular momentum of the object with respect to origin, when it reaches at the maximum height, will be [ g is acceleration due to gravity]"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{m v_o^3}{2 \\sqrt{2} g}$ along negative $z$-axis",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{m v_o^3}{4 \\sqrt{2} g}$ along positive $z$-axis",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{m v_o^3}{4 \\sqrt{2} g}$ along negative $z$-axis",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{m v_o^3}{2 \\sqrt{2} g}$ along positive $z$-axis",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0040_2a0752e7bd52.png\"><br>\n\n\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{H}=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{v}_0}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^2}{2 \\mathrm{~g}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{v}_0^2}{4 \\mathrm{~g}} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~L}=\\mathrm{mvh} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~L}=\\mathrm{m} \\frac{\\mathrm{v}_0}{\\sqrt{2}} \\frac{\\mathrm{v}_0^2}{4 \\mathrm{~g}}\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
